here are a few moments completely out of  context from tatsuki fujimoto's chainsaw  man a headless turkey becomes the school  pet for a group of high school students  a girl is forced to play DDR while  having a full-scale panic attack there's  a tournament for kicking a man in the  balls a guy made of chainsaws rides a  shark like a horse using chainsaw chains  as Reigns in order to fight a giant baby  from a glance chainsaw man looks like a  story derived by someone utterly [ __ ]  deranged  it's hyperviolent page is soaked with  copious amounts of blood and gore  accompanied by the kind of humor you'd  expect to hear in a freshman High School  class Playing Cards Against Humanity but  in between the moments of insanity  the violence the crudeness is the kind  of heart and sincerity that has brought  me back to its Pages again and again a  Shonen story with a pulpiness and  texture that makes the series stand  apart from its contemporaries and Shonen  jump and now with the anime by Studio  map of Jujutsu kaisen Fame right around  the corner and a lot of new fans finding  out about the series for the first time  I wanted to sit down and really talk  about it I'm red Muffler Man  and today I'd like to introduce you to  the sincere insanity  chainsaw man and why you need to watch  it  [Music]  chainsaw man began its run in weekly  Shonen Jump in 2018 and was the  brainchild of one tatsuki fujimota  Fujimoto at the time had been known for  his work on the manga fire punch in  2016. a series known for  being [ __ ] batshit  to give an example Fire Punch opens in a  world which has been thrown into a  second Ice Age and the main character  has the ability of endless regeneration  which he uses to cut off body parts in  order to provide food for the people of  his village as well as his sister who is  uh kinda into him  uh his village is slaughtered by the  government for being cannibals and our  protagonist is then set on fire by a guy  whose ability is to summon infinitely  burning flames which causes our main  character to burn endlessly  however his powers of regeneration keep  him alive even through the pain from  there he blazes a path through the snowy  Wasteland on a literally and  figuratively burning quest for vengeance  I've known writers who have used subtext  and they are all cowards  fujimoto's work on fire punches  fantastic and honestly I might make a  video about it one day but needless to  say it perfectly exemplified fujimoto's  style of Storytelling stories of uncanny  broken people going through absolutely  insane situations people that despite  everything they have gone through or the  things they've done are still very human  and after cutting his teeth in the pages  of Jump Plus with fire punch Fujimoto  began his serialization of Chainsaw man  in the pages of weakly Shonen Jump  chainsaw man is the story of denji a  broke kid who through a series of  incredibly Unfortunate Events has been  thrown into a debt from the Yakuza  singing to the tune of roughly 38  million yen which totals to about 250  Grand in US dollars  to work off this insane debt denji Works  a variety of odd jobs  he cuts down trees sells his kidneys his  left eye his uh  testicles oh God we're gonna get  demonetized but by denji's side he has a  single friend pachta a dog-like creature  with a chainsaw sticking out of his face  and together the two of them attempt to  pay back that debt hunting Devils now  devils are essentially a race of  supernatural beings that feed upon the  fears of humanity so if you have  something that you're afraid of there's  probably a devil for it you have Devils  ranging from the Cockroach devil the  fish devil the Tomato devil the sea  cucumber devil the chicken devil  okay yeah this is the part of the video  where I tell you  yes  I know I called him a turkey at the  start of the video  that was to purposely bait you into  leaving comments telling me that I was  wrong in order to boost the engagement  on this video  if you fell for it then just know  I am always  one  Step Ahead  but devils in the world of Chainsaw man  can range from just minor inconveniences  in a household to brickingly apocalyptic  hell spawn and so it's up to devil  Hunters to act as a kind of  extermination Squad to keep them in  check so denji risks life and limb every  day to get the bounties for killing  these Devils of which nearly everything  he makes is taken from him by the Yakuza  for his debts leaving denji with barely  the money to even buy a loaf of bread  dingy situation has gotten so bad that  ideas like being able to eat toast with  Jam in the morning or to be able to talk  to a girl all of these feel like  astronomical Feats that he would never  be able to achieve in his lifetime  denji lives a life of Despair but since  despair is all he's ever known it's  something he's become accustomed to  and so denji dreams  because the world has taken everything  from him  but no one  can take away his dreams  but Dengue and pochita just can't catch  a break and after being lured into a  trap set by the Yakuza both denji and  pochita were murdered  left for dead inside of a dumpster  but in their final moments  the two combined with one another in  order to stay alive with pochita the  chainsaw devil acting as denji's heart  newly awakened denji becomes chainsaw  man a being neither human nor devil  but something  in between  from here denji is found by the  mysterious makima a woman working with  the Japanese government for a division  of devil Hunters  she gives denji an ultimatum to either  be hunted down and killed as a devil or  to be her lap dog to hunt Devils as a  human  Genji accepts and begins his new life in  Tokyo as a professional devil Hunter  denji's Journey from the pit of despair  is  pretty touching but what really sets him  apart in my eyes from your dekus your  tanjiros your Luffy's is that denji  really acts his age  he acts like a head teenager he's crude  he's awkward and blunt with people Genji  will say some of the most  cringe-inducing [ __ ] like challenging a  devil to a dream battle or agreeing to  kill a devil if it means he gets to make  out with one of his co-workers he's not  trying to be some hero of Justice or  trying to avenge the death of his family  or anything Noble like that  stupid kid living up the life that was  taken from him he lives by his own set  of morals so whenever he does something  that anyone else in the story thinks is  insane to him it makes perfect sense  it's always a blast to see what sort of  insane idea denji comes up with in the  middle of a fight and then hearing the  bat insane justification for it and then  being like  that actually makes sense what the [ __ ]  but denji also has a real  Human Side to him there are moments of  introspection in denji's Journey that  have kept me up at night  to give some context I'd like to talk  about a small scene from the manga there  are some minor spoilers so if you would  like to avoid them please skip ahead to  the time stamp I've listed below  in this scene denji has just defeated  the leech devil and rescued Power one of  his devil hunting co-workers in order to  thank him for this power lets him uh  cup of feel  no no no no don't leave I I promise this  is going somewhere  a cop a fee  this is something Dengue has dreamed of  for a long time and  he did it  he lived his dream  but  he's not happy  there's no joy  denji just feels  empty  the thing he had dreamed of for so long  was nothing like what he thought it  would be  that the journey to get to that point in  his life  felt kind of meaningless  and now that he'd achieved that dream he  felt lost  with no goal in sight  I think about this scene  a lot  I've had a lot of Dreams in my life that  I've worked insanely hard to achieve  grinding myself to the point of absolute  burnout Knights of crying to myself  silently wondering if the pain of it all  is even worth it or if I'm even good  enough and then even when you make it  you find out there is  no such thing as making it that you  never stop chasing that the goals you  hold Aloft so high at the end of the day  will feel empty when you finally grasp  them in your hands  when I read this I had to stop for a  good 30 minutes as I kinda just  sat there  one of the biggest struggles I had ever  felt in my life as a young adult  had been laid perfectly bare to me in  less than five pages  [Music]  then I remember this scene is about  boobs  these moments of sincere introspection  are littered all throughout the story of  Chainsaw man you can feel the years of  lived experiences that Fujimoto puts  into the pages of this story and it  makes denji feel so very  real  and it's not just dingy the entire cast  of Chainsaw man has a real texture to  them all of them with their own sets of  morals and beliefs their own motivations  for doing the things that they do  for example Aki who serves as the main  foil to denji is single-mindedly focused  on a thirst for vengeance but over time  begins to develop a soft spot for the  comrades he fights with  as such  struggles with the fact that he's using  the people around him for his own goals  power who on the surface appears to just  be a mad serial killer but only acts so  because it's the only life she's ever  known cobeni who is just  normal  but has to deal with the fact that the  world she lives in is insanely [ __ ] up  I love her she's my favorite yes I'm  very basic and makima who takes the  supernatural in stride acting as an  observer to the world around her even  the smallest of Side characters have  some of the most insane backstories and  motivations imaginable such as cosmos  whose literal only character traits are  that she can only say the word Halloween  and she is a lesbian and then it turns  out she has the most metal backstory  ever holy  so [ __ ] cool but that texture that  sincerity it makes getting close to  these characters feel more like getting  close to real living people it makes it  feel so when something crazy happens  those moments feel real no matter how  insane things get you're invested and it  also makes the story  that much more heartbreaking when these  characters whom we've grown so close  with are  suddenly ripped away I'm not going to  beat around the bush  chainsaw man for every moment of  insanity or close introspection or  off-color humor or insane violent  spectacle we'll have another moment of  sheer heartbreak and Terror  at any moment a character can be killed  on sanctimoniously  no Flags  no warning  just death many times the death won't  even register with you at first  just like in real life it's  sudden  then the realization hits  slowly not just for our cast but  for the audience  the theme of death is ever present in  the pages of Chainsaw man  and while that can sometimes be a downer  it's also one of the places where  fujimoto's art style  truly shines  Fujimoto renders his characters to be  closer to what one would expect from  real human anatomy rather than having  them look more in line with traditional  anime while at times this can lead to  his characters looking somewhat uncanny  it also means that Fujimoto can play  with the expressiveness of his  characters  this can lead to moments of pure  Euphoria painted all over a character's  face or much more likely  the feeling of Terror and Dread of  having to face how cruel the world can  be  this expressive visual design also  carries over to the look and feel of the  Devils a majority of the devils are  these surreal pictures of body horror  looking just human enough in their  appearance to elicit a feeling of  discomfort that something is obviously  wrong that this thing  was once a person  from the strange imagery of a  decapitated head walking around with a  foot and hand sticking out of its neck  to a woman wearing a dead smile made of  countless sets of arms or even dengie's  bloody industrial transformation into  chainsaw man gives the show an unnerving  edge that only adds to its brand of  Horror  and one thing I can say for sure about  the anime is that the trailers seem to  be taking this visual style and Running  With It characters are just as  expressive as they are in the manga if  not more so and the dark color palette  sells the mood of the show incredibly  well the few action shots we've seen  from the trailers have been ridiculously  over animated Feats of pure sakuga the  hell every episode of the first 13  episode core will have its own ending  credits animation not to mention the  staff behind this anime are All-Stars  Studio mapa of Jujutsu kaisen Fame also  who famously overworked their animators  because the Japanese animation industry  is fundamentally broken music composed  by kensuke ushio who did the scores for  Devilman crybaby a silent voice and ping  pong the animation as well as a slew of  other incredibly talented artists who  have worked on everything from SSS  gridman Mobile Suit Gundam ironplated  orphans mob psycho 100 Space Dandy flip  flappers bro you need to watch flip  Flappers oh my God everything about the  adaptation for chainsaw man is leading  me to believe that it is going to be the  next big thing in anime and it's why I  implore you if you're on the fence  please give the show shot or Hell read  the Manga which recently came off of  Hiatus and still continues to make me  laugh but has also unnerved me to my  absolute core there's not been a day  that has gone by since January of 2021  that I've not thought about this story  at least once you need  to watch chainsaw man  thank you so much for watching as per  usual if you like everything we do on  the channel feel free to drop a like a  comment and hit that subscribe button  and if you like me and what I do you can  follow me on Twitch Twitter and YouTube  and red Muffler Man I'm incredibly happy  I got to talk about the story with you  today and I really honestly hope you  give it 